| `CachedNetworkId` resolution | `src/engine/shared/library/sharedObject/src/shared/object/CachedNetworkId.cpp:150-177` | Only calls hash lookup when `isValid()`; no sign/range narrowing. | SAFE | SAFE |
| `Watcher` side of cached ids | `CachedNetworkId.cpp:170-177`; `CachedNetworkId.h:68` | Cached pointer is a `Watcher<Object>`; identity is pointer after first lookup, full id before lookup. | SAFE | SAFE |
| Cluster-id bit packing | `NetworkId.cpp:19-32`, `:81-87`, `:92-107` | Layout: bit 63 sign/buildout; bit 62 client fake; bits 61..54 cluster id; bits 53..0 object id. Values `<= 0x3fffffffffffff` are treated unclustered. `getValueWithoutClusterId()` masks with `0x403fffffffffffff`, preserving fake bit and low 54 bits, clearing sign and cluster bits only on values above max. | SAFE: negative signed compare returns unchanged and cluster id `0`. | SAFE only for `0x80000000..0x3fffffffffffff`; RISK/BLOCKER above that because cluster bits can be interpreted/masked. |
