| Network serialization | `NetworkIdArchive.cpp:49-63`; `CachedNetworkIdArchive.h:17-28` | `NetworkId` serializes 8-byte `int64`. `CachedNetworkIdArchive` uses `uint64` raw bits but stores back into signed id; no 32-bit truncation. | SAFE locally/protocol-width-wise | SAFE locally/protocol-width-wise |
| `.ws` allocator seeding | `WorldSnapshot.cpp:1906-1911`, `:1937-1942`, `:1967-1977`, `:1996-2007`; config guard `:2468-2479` | Allocator band is positive and `<= INT32_MAX`; seed ignores reader ids `>= ceiling`; collision scan only walks `[seed, ceiling)`. Client-only `.ilf` ids are not in `ms_reader`. | SAFE/excluded | SAFE if above `INT32_MAX`; cannot enter allocator band due config guard. |
| `.ws` persistence width | `WorldSnapshotReaderWriter.cpp:430-431`, `:462-463`, `:496-497`; save gate `WorldSnapshot.cpp:2602-2612` | On-disk `.ws` ids are int32; editor save refuses ids `<=0` or `>INT32_MAX` for authored nodes. | SAFE only if `.ilf` ids never become `.ws` nodes; BLOCKER if promoted into `.ws`. | Same: BLOCKER if promoted into `.ws`. |
